.TH F 1 Blit
.SH NAME
f \- font conversion program
.SH SYNOPSIS
jx
.B f
<
.I script
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I f
is an mpx program that accepts fonts in either Blit or Mergenthaler
format and can write Blit or
Canon (Versatec) format fonts.
.I f
reads standard input (N.B. jx standard input can
.I not
be from the keyboard) until EOF or a character is typed.  Subsequent input
is taken from the keyboard.
Normally
.I f
is used to make several Blit font files, each with a specific point size, from
one Mergenthaler archive.  This is reasonable since converting Mergenthaler
characters is much faster than reading them in.
.PP
Conversion takes place using a Mergenthaler simulation modified for extremely
small point sizes.  For this reason
.I f
uses a
.I rational
specification of point size.  For example, to generate a 10 point Canon font
one would choose a pair of numbers whose ratio is (972*32)/(240*10), where
972 is the Mergenthaler resolution, 32 is the default Mergenthaler point
size, and 240 is the resolution of the Canon printer.  To specify this
point size one could say any of "p 1 13", "p 2 26", "p 3 40", or any other
combination of numbers with the proper ratio and some magical numerical
properties.  (One chooses these numbers by looking at the results as well
as calculating what they should be.)
.PP
f commands:
.TP +3
i \fIfile\fP
include file
.TP
f \fIn\fP
select font n [0 <= n < 10]
.TP
s	(skip) add empty character to selected font
.TP
merg \fIfile\fP
read in a Mergenthaler character
.TP
p \fIn m\fP
set rational point size
.TP
space \fIn\fP
set intercharacter spacing
.TP
r	(reduce) add converted character to selected font
.TP
can \fIfile\fP
write Versatec font to file
.TP
e \fIfile\fP
read Blit font from file
.TP
w \fIfile\fP
write Blit font to file
.TP
q	exit
.SH FILES
/usr/jerq/include/font.h	Blit font format
.SH BUGS
A font index must not be more than 1 larger than the previous largest font
index.
.br
Static charge can type a key and stop the program.
